Chapter: CapIdentityDenied

 Runtime probe for the identity capability: the key syscalls (15
 load, 16 zero, 18 status) consult the per-process capability word
 before touching the pinned identity key. The program declares
 Identity, so the boot grant derived from its own manifest includes
 the identity bit: it loads a key (status flips to 1), zeros it
 (status back to 0), then strips its own grant word and asks again.
 The kernel refuses with -1 without touching the key region.

Section: Body

  proc0-cap-addr : Integer = 20536

  strip-grant : Integer -> Integer
  strip-grant (x) =
    let lo = poke-32 proc0-cap-addr 0 0
    in let hi = poke-32 proc0-cap-addr 4 0
    in 0

  opening : [Console, Identity] Nothing = act
    loaded <- key-load (alloc-bytes 32)
    st1 <- key-status
    print-line-uni ("loaded: " & show loaded & " status: " & show st1)
    zeroed <- key-zero
    st2 <- key-status
    print-line-uni ("zeroed: " & show zeroed & " status: " & show st2)
    print-line-uni ("stripped: " & show (strip-grant 0))
    st3 <- key-status
    print-line-uni ("denied: " & show st3)
  end
